      "tree": {
        "sha": "c95b1075855d4f22f555be5ab54ca6720d14c234",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/c95b1075855d4f22f555be5ab54ca6720d14c234"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree c95b1075855d4f22f555be5ab54ca6720d14c234\nparent b3682ac7eb18e5a9560e263681942cac3ac252f3\nauthor ViniciusCestarii <viniciuscestari01@gmail.com> 1795608908 -0300\ncommitter ViniciusCestarii <viniciuscestari01@gmail.com> 1795640718 -0300\n\ninterfaces: add Events interface\n\nAdd a pull-based stream of chain and mempool events (block connected,\nblock disconnected, transaction added to and removed from the\nmempool). Each subscription chooses which event types it wants and\nwhether to include the serialized block or transaction.\n\nEvents are buffered on the node side from the moment the interface is\ncreated, so a slow client never slows down the node. The buffer is\nlimited by the new -ipceventsbuffer option. When it is full, the\noldest events are dropped and the client sees a gap in the per\nsubscription Event::sequence. waitNext acknowledges events up to\n\"after\" and returns a batch limited by max_events and MAX_BATCH_BYTES.\n\nThe mutex and condition variable live in KernelNotifications so that\nInterrupt() can wake pending waitNext calls on shutdown.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgY7NROixtPE3hjThUiBvdMFhx+5\nJyj1M7a6RXrjRGqmMAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCTIzpuznwi1AmnrcASgCPDfPNQj/Tz68IIPKLr4py/ZgcJoeM3TruduYw9bdFAJkY\naw2p0eJ00vkoPvNZm/Yws=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----"
      },
      "parents": [
        {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/b3682ac7eb18e5a9560e263681942cac3ac252f3",
          "sha": "b3682ac7eb18e5a9560e263681942cac3ac252f3",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/b3682ac7eb18e5a9560e263681942cac3ac252f3"
        }
      ],
      "message": "interfaces: add Events interface\n\nAdd a pull-based stream of chain and mempool events (block connected,\nblock disconnected, transaction added to and removed from the\nmempool). Each subscription chooses which event types it wants and\nwhether to include the serialized block or transaction.\n\nEvents are buffered on the node side from the moment the interface is\ncreated, so a slow client never slows down the node. The buffer is\nlimited by the new -ipceventsbuffer option. When it is full, the\noldest events are dropped and the client sees a gap in the per\nsubscription Event::sequence. waitNext acknowledges events up to\n\"after\" and returns a batch limited by max_events and MAX_BATCH_BYTES.\n\nThe mutex and condition variable live in KernelNotifications so that\nInterrupt() can wake pending waitNext calls on shutdown.",
